---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { site } from "../../data/site.js";
---
<BaseLayout title="About CyberLearn Lab">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="container">
    <div class="breadcrumb">ABOUT</div>
    <h1>Learning through research and practice</h1>
    <p>{site.name} is an independent educational project created to make complex technology concepts easier to understand through clear explanations and practical experimentation.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="container" style="max-width:850px">
    <div class="article">
      <h2>About the platform</h2>
      <p>CyberLearn Lab explores cybersecurity, cryptography, artificial intelligence, blockchain, digital forensics and related technologies. The aim is to connect foundational theory with implementation, experimentation and responsible practice.</p>
      <h2>About the creator</h2>
      <p>Created by Dr Kasun Moolikagedara, whose academic and professional interests span AI security, blockchain, computer vision, network and information security, and secure technology operations.</p>
      <p>Kasun Moolikagedara completed a PhD in Computer Science at Auckland University of Technology in 2024. His research explored blockchain-based video integrity frameworks for intelligent surveillance, with connections to computer vision and digital media authenticity. He also holds an MSc in Network & Information Security from Kingston University, UK.</p>
      <h2>Learning philosophy</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Explain the concept before introducing complexity.</li>
        <li>Connect theory to practical examples.</li>
        <li>Use interactive demonstrations where they add real learning value.</li>
        <li>Encourage ethical, safe and responsible experimentation.</li>
        <li>Reference reliable standards, research and further reading.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Connect</h2>
      <p>Visit the <a class="card-link" href="https://ktvshwajith.github.io/portfolio-KasunM/">professional portfolio</a> for background, research and contact information.</p>
    </div>
  </div></section>
</BaseLayout>
